WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome back to the show.
-Thank you, Seth.

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:03.003 line:92%
-Very happy to have you here.

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:06.606
Obviously this is a book
about endangered species,

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:07.841 size:78% position:39%
and you've been doing
a lot of traveling,

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:10.477
going to different zoos,
and I want to show you a photo.

00:00:10.477 --> 00:00:13.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
You met a -- what kind of --
the hellbender.

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:14.814 size:81% position:41%
-A hellbender, we did.
-What is a hellbender?

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:17.183
-A very large salamander.
-A very large salamander.

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:22.322
And I will say, hellbender,
not an attractive animal, but --

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:23.056 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Cute in its own way.

00:00:23.056 --> 00:00:25.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I will say, you're giving
best effort there.

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:26.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-It actually was --

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:28.795
Okay, it was a little slimy,
but it also was quite soft.

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:32.632
-Yes, and then who is this,
your friend that touched it?

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:33.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
Who is this that
I'm about to show you?

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:36.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you know?
Because she is not --

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:38.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my God!
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:40.740 line:92%
-She does not seem as happy.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's Joy.
-That's Joy?

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:43.610 line:92%
-Oh, my gosh. I'm so sorry, Joy.

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:46.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
I didn't know this was gonna
happen tonight.

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:46.579 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:50.150
-I feel like you're someone
who's just been in politics

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:50.850 size:81% position:41% line:92%
a lot longer than Joy.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're like, no matter
whose hand you're shaking,

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:54.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
you've got to look like
you're engaged.

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:55.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, and look at Mark,
the keeper,

00:00:55.855 --> 00:00:59.793
who has, like, really taken on
trying to save the hellbenders.

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:01.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
They've released 6,000
into the wild.

00:01:01.161 --> 00:01:03.463
They're a huge part of what
the St. Louis Zoo is doing.

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:06.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, like, look at Mark.
-And Joy just sells him out.

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:07.467 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:09.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Joy just, I guess, wasn't up
for it. Oh, my God.

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:12.072
-You know, I think it's very --
-May I take that?

00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:14.808
-Yeah, you can have that.
Of course, there you go.

00:01:14.808 --> 00:01:16.576 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thank you.

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:20.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think there are just
a litany of things

00:01:20.814 --> 00:01:22.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
that are getting
lost in the shuffle

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:24.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
as far as what's going on with
the current administration.

00:01:24.951 --> 00:01:27.687
Conservation is obviously
a huge -- one of those.

00:01:27.687 --> 00:01:30.156 size:84% position:42%
Are you -- Obviously,
you're doing your best.

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:33.159
But do you feel like this is
an issue that not only do people

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:37.330
not realize how serious it is,
but also based on the noise,

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:38.131 line:92%
is impossible to focus on?

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:40.200
-Yeah, I think that a lot of
people don't know how much

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.969
the Trump administration has
done to roll back protections

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:43.703 size:84% position:42% line:92%
for endangered species.

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:45.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, they weakened
the Endangered Species Act.

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:50.710
It's now legal to bring elephant
and lion carcasses and trophies

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:51.644 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
into the country.

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:55.615
They're planning on opening the
Arctic wildlife natural refuge

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:56.483 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
to oil drilling.

00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:58.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
That would be devastating
for polar bears.

00:01:58.618 --> 00:02:01.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
They tried to re-legalize
grizzly bear hunting

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:03.223 line:92%
in Yellowstone National Park,

00:02:03.223 --> 00:02:05.258
something that hadn't been done
in more than 40 years.

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:08.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
So they're really, you know,
pushing back

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:10.296 size:78% position:39%
on endangered species
wherever they can.

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:12.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And how do you even
try to explain to people

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:16.569
how serious this is when it
strikes me that, you know --

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:17.670 line:92%
You've lived in the White House.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:20.173 line:92%
This one seems pretty chaotic.

00:02:20.173 --> 00:02:21.174 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, you think?

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:21.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:23.743
-I mean, I would imagine
because of your experience,

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:24.611 line:92%
you would say to certain people

00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:26.779
who have an expectation of what
happens during a presidency,

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:29.649
like, "Trust me, it's a lot
harder than you think it is.

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:30.550 line:92%
There's a lot more going on."

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:32.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are you constantly
taken aback, however,

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:35.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
by exactly how chaotic
this one seems?

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:37.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Okay.

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:40.894
-And by the new levels of
cruelty that this administration

00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:43.329 size:81% position:41%
seems to find, whether
it's with the children

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:45.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
being separated from
their families at the border

00:02:45.532 --> 00:02:47.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
or it's with
the Endangered Species Act,

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:51.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
which had never really been
controversial before.

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:51.504 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:52.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, passed, like,
pretty unanimously,

00:02:52.872 --> 00:02:56.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
signed by President
Richard Nixon, of all people.

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:57.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yep. Yeah.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:01.381 size:88% position:44%
-And yet Trump has made
this controversial, too.

00:03:01.381 --> 00:03:03.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right. He believes
that if you're endangered,

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:05.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
you did something wrong.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.285 --> 00:03:07.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, and his sons
like to hunt.

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:08.021 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Yeah, they are hunters.

00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:10.356
-So I think, kind of, that's
the beginning and the end.

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:13.493
-I would've hoped that if his
sons did it, he would hate it,

00:03:13.493 --> 00:03:16.029
and this would be one that would
work in our favor,

00:03:16.029 --> 00:03:19.065
but it turns out they're on
the same page on this one.

00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:19.666 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Unfortunately.

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:25.071
-I also want to ask -- it must
be very strange that Fox News --

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:26.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know if you know,
it's a channel --

00:03:26.806 --> 00:03:28.141 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:29.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't watch it.
I am aware of it.

00:03:29.309 --> 00:03:31.511
-Yes, you're aware of it,
but you probably are also aware

00:03:31.511 --> 00:03:37.984
that your family is still a
topic of obsession for Fox News.

00:03:37.984 --> 00:03:38.618 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Are you surprised?

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:41.921
Is your mother aware that you
guys are still, sort of --

00:03:41.921 --> 00:03:44.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Living rent free
in their heads.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:44.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yes.

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:48.895 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
I do find it bewildering.

00:03:48.895 --> 00:03:53.066
I will say if it consumes
time and oxygen to allow

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:55.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
the Democrats in the House
and the Senate,

00:03:55.602 --> 00:03:58.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
and in the state houses
and legislatures

00:03:58.338 --> 00:03:59.439 line:92%
to actually get real work done,

00:03:59.439 --> 00:04:01.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess I could be
okay with that.

00:04:01.107 --> 00:04:02.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, if they're
still obsessing about

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:04.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
my mother's walking
in the woods...

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:04.944 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.944 --> 00:04:07.280 align:start size:94% position:6%
...and it allows Democrats
to actually try to stop

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:10.350
bad things from happening,
and make progress elsewhere,

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:11.884 line:92%
like, I can live with that.

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:16.356
But I do sometimes wonder, like,
if my mother weren't here --

00:04:16.356 --> 00:04:19.359
and I hope she's here for many,
many, many decades to come,

00:04:19.359 --> 00:04:21.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, what would they
talk about?

00:04:21.094 --> 00:04:22.629 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.629 --> 00:04:23.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
It'd be very strange.
-Yes.

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:26.199 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It would just -- like,
"We're back from commercial,

00:04:26.199 --> 00:04:28.334
and we're gonna have another one
in five minutes,

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:33.373
and just go about your business,
and we'll go about ours."

00:04:33.373 --> 00:04:35.141 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.141 --> 00:04:38.811
I want to ask you, as well.
You have another one on the way.

00:04:38.811 --> 00:04:39.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
How are the --
-Yes.

00:04:39.746 --> 00:04:42.815
-Congratulations.
-Thank you very much. Thank you.

00:04:42.815 --> 00:04:43.983 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:45.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
-2 and 4 now?
-2 and 4.

00:04:45.785 --> 00:04:49.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How are 2- and 4-year-olds
reacting to the news?

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:50.490 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Are they excited?

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:53.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, our daughter Charlotte
is really excited.

00:04:53.026 --> 00:04:54.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-She loves being a big sister.

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:57.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think admittedly she partly
loves being a big sister

00:04:57.997 --> 00:05:00.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause her little brother
adores her.

00:05:00.433 --> 00:05:01.367 line:92%
-Oh, there you go. Right.

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:02.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
Build her fan base.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:05:02.969 --> 00:05:06.039
I think she sees this as, like,
someone else to adore her.

00:05:06.039 --> 00:05:08.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
But she is a really good,
generous-hearted big sister.

00:05:08.708 --> 00:05:10.743
I think, though, Aidan is
mainly excited, again --

00:05:10.743 --> 00:05:13.946
like, see previous comment about
his adoration of his big sister,

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:15.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
because his big sister
is excited.

00:05:15.381 --> 00:05:17.750
So every day Charlotte wants to,
like, touch my belly,

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:20.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
see if she can feel the baby,
talk about the baby,

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:22.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then Aidan
will sort of clue in

00:05:22.355 --> 00:05:25.425 line:92%
and be like, "Baby! Yes!"

00:05:25.425 --> 00:05:27.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And how are your parents
as grandparents?

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:30.897
I mean, I know you're obviously,
you know,

00:05:30.897 --> 00:05:32.165 line:92%
you're gonna grade them well,

00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:34.467 align:start size:94% position:6%
but do you feel like
they're doing a good job?

00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:36.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think they're doing
a really good job.

00:05:36.636 --> 00:05:38.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're really involved,
which I love.

00:05:38.204 --> 00:05:41.908
And I love watching them read
and sing and play with our kids.

00:05:41.908 --> 00:05:43.643 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I definitely have, like,

00:05:43.643 --> 00:05:45.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
really dropped on
the ladder of importance.

00:05:45.745 --> 00:05:46.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:48.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Like, whole conversations now
happen while I will have

00:05:48.715 --> 00:05:51.551
hung up the phone or gotten off
Facetime, and I'm like,

00:05:51.551 --> 00:05:53.086 line:92%
"They never asked how I was."

00:05:53.086 --> 00:05:53.619 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.619 --> 00:05:54.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's okay.
-I think that happens.

00:05:54.954 --> 00:05:57.256
I think that happens everywhere.
-Natural order. Yeah.

00:05:57.256 --> 00:05:59.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you, as always,
for being here.

00:05:59.125 --> 00:05:59.926 line:92%
Thanks for writing the book.

00:05:59.926 --> 00:06:01.994 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you, Seth.
Thank you so much. Thank you.

00:06:01.994 --> 00:06:03.896 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's Chelsea Clinton,
everybody.

